# Tuncay Gezer Atelier — Cursor Rules
# Architecture: Feature-Sliced Design + Next.js App Router + Strict TypeScript

## CORE RULES

### TypeScript
- ZERO use of `any` type — use `unknown`, proper generics, or specific types
- Strict null checks enabled — always handle null/undefined explicitly
- All function parameters and return types must be explicitly typed
- Prefer `interface` over `type` for object shapes
- Use Zod for runtime validation of external data

### Next.js App Router
- Mark all interactive components with `'use client'` directive at the top
- Server Components by default — only use client where needed (state, effects, browser APIs)
- Use `next/image` for all images with explicit width/height
- All API routes must use typed `NextRequest`/`NextResponse`

### React
- Always clean up useEffect subscriptions (return teardown function)
- Prefer `useCallback` for event handlers passed to children
- Never use inline object/array literals as props (causes re-render)
- Use `useRef` for DOM manipulation, not `useState`

### GSAP & Animation
- Always kill ScrollTrigger instances in useEffect cleanup
- Always revert Split-Type instances in cleanup
- Pin GSAP timelines to component lifecycle

### FSD Directory Compliance
- `app/` — Next.js routing only
- `features/` — Self-contained feature slices with their own components/hooks
- `shared/lib/` — Pure utilities, no React components
- `shared/types/` — All TypeScript interfaces and Zod schemas
- `public/` — Static assets only

### Performance
- GPU-accelerate animations with `will-change: transform` only when animating
- Remove `will-change` after animations complete
- Target 60+ FPS on all interactive canvas elements
- Lazy-load Three.js components with dynamic import

### Naming
- Components: PascalCase
- Hooks: camelCase with `use` prefix
- Utils: camelCase
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE
- CSS classes: kebab-case
